{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>Where is the matter of 'one of my mother's sons' who said: We have a little sister, what shall we do for our sister on the day she is spoken of for marriage? If she guarded herself and she is a wall, we will build upon it a turret of silver, and the matter is connected; and if she is a door, we will barricade upon it a cedar plank (and she will be shut up:" "She said: I am a wall, and my breasts are like towers (as in the sense of) שדים נכונו:" "Then I was in the eyes of my beloveds as one who finds peace:" "<b>The third time</b><br>We have a little sister. When Israel ascends, then they will say one to another: We have a little sister, and they are the two and a half tribes who were exiled first, as stated: כעת הראשון הקל ארצה זבולון וארצה נפתלי וגו׳." "And she has no breasts. Perhaps she has no Torahs:" "On the day she is spoken of. When she stands in judgment:"], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:04.734166821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}